  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W35_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-35",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W35_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-35.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-09-01",
  "report_week": "35",
  "report_period": "Week 35 (25th Aug to 1st Sep 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Mitsubishi Ore Transport have committed their Capesize \"Santa Lucia\" 176/2006 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 08/2026, DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) to Turkish buyers Beks for excess USD 16 mill. Remind you that back in June, the \"Atlantic Tiger\" 180/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024) was sold at USD 16,85 mill. In addition, Chinese owners sold the \"Xin Wang Hai\" 174/2003 SWS, China (SS/DD 10/2023) to compatriots for USD 12,8 mill. The Ultramax \"Lowlands Breeze\" 61/2013 Iwagi, Japan (SS 07/2028, DD 07/2026, BWTS fitted) of Fukusei Sangyo was committed to Greek buyers for high USD 20 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"CL Ebisu\" 61/2014 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at high USD 26 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Sea Aquarius\" 53/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS 05/2026, DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold to Chinese buyers for high USD 9 mill. Note that the one-year-younger \"Tai Honesty\" 55/2007 Oshima, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in July at low USD 12 mill. The OHBS Handysize \"Steady Sarah\" 38/2011 Minami-Nippon, Japan (SS 05/2026, DD 09/2023, BWTS fitted) was committed to UK buyers for USD 15 mill, while the two-years-younger \"Nord Savannah\" 37/2013 Saiki, Japan (SS 05/2028, DD 05/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 16,5 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel of the latter \"Cielo Di Palermo\" 37/2013 Saiki, Japan (SS 08/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 17 mill. Moreover, the conventional \"Tasman Spirit\" 35/2010 Nantong, China (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at USD 9,5 mill. Note that back in May, the sister vessel \"Ithaca Stockholm\" 35/2010 Nantong, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 11 mill.",
    "tankers": "Lila Global have committed their Suezmax \"Lila Orlando\" 158/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS 06/2025, DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) to Chinese buyers for high USD 37 mill. Remind you that the \"Classic\" 159/2005 Hyundai, Korea (SS 10/2025, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at USD 36,75 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 7,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 7,000/10,000 pd range. A number of Indonesia and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/700K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 11,000 pd basis delivery China for 6/8 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 9,000/12,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 12,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 16,000/17,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,500/18,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 175K/185K. Trips from Black Sea into China were fixed around usd 19,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/600K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of trips from China into India with steels were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into Persian Gulf were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips into North Coast South America were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. South American trips into Continent with alumina were fixed around usd 15,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
